  "limitations": [
    "Reviewed by a fresh read-only `codex exec` invoked by hand, not by `xtask review`: the controller's predecessor gate refuses P09 subjects until C26 completes; D058 and the owner's 2026-10-26 instruction authorise proceeding. Receipts are regenerated through the controller once C26 completes.",
    "The working tree holds the owner's uncommitted C26 attempt-02 and academy-2.1 work, excluded from scope; the input inventory covers the compiled and tested sources.",
    "`xtask check`/`xtask test` as whole commands were not run (they would include the owner's in-progress work); their constituent commands relevant to this chunk were run individually with exit codes and log hashes recorded.",
    "The chunk's work is committed as f0a1a61a (HEAD); scope and diff.patch are measured from HEAD~1, plus the uncommitted parity notes. Native acceptance C35-N01..N03 recorded against the rebuilt fixture bundle (native-prepare.json; executable hash bound in native-acceptance.json) with AX trees, self-captures and the layout matrix under evidence/C35/screens: the rail (destinations with \u2318 hints, the Administration products as children with the New tag, hidden and shown by the chevron), the status block (Connected with the read status, Harness, Keychain, Jobs, Settings \u2318, opening Settings, the theme toggle switching the shown appearance), the header (title, the 260px search button, the Explain switch flipping the show-the-calls preference and its panel, Ask Harness opening the Harness), the 360px tenant menu and the 640px palette with their rows and keys, Tab order, the focus ring, and 1440\u00d7900 plus 900\u00d7600 at 200% in both themes with no horizontal overflow.",
    "Visual parity (D059, docs/planning/p09-recut.md): the composites under docs/planning/evidence/C35/parity (prototype board left, fixture app right, 1440\u00d7800) were judged and approved by the owner on 2026-10-29 (parity/notes.md records the approval and the deviations); the review scores the implementation against the chunk brief and the specification, not the pixels.",
    "C35 has no live row: synthetic scan and management endpoints only. Rust suite ui_v2_shell_port pins the catalogue, inventory and preference contract the shell reads; the component suite v2-shell.test.tsx covers the rail, header, tenant menu (incl. \u2303n) and palette. Acceptance threshold for this chunk is 8 (D032/D034, D059).",
    "Timing-sensitive tests outside this chunk are retried on the same frozen inputs when they flake under full-suite load; any core-fixtures.flake-N.log or host.flake-N.log retained records such a retry (the host flakes are the Academy device-flow tests in browser_callback.rs, untouched by C35)."
